    "legal_toc_section_gYznx3": {
      "type": "legal-toc-section",
      "blocks": {
        "content_section_GLa7AN": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Introduction",
            "title": "1. Introduction and scope",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>This policy explains what we collect about you, why we need it, who helps us process it, and how you stay in control.</strong></p><p>KARMICA BV (“KARMICARE”, “we”, “us” or “our”) respects your fundamental right to privacy and is committed to protecting your personal data in full compliance with:</p><ul><li>The <strong>General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679</strong> (“GDPR”);</li><li>The <strong>Belgian Data Protection Act of 30 July 2018;</strong></li><li>The <strong>Belgian Electronic Communications Act of 13 June 2005</strong>, transposing the ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC as amended;</li><li>Applicable international privacy legislation, including the <strong>UK GDPR</strong> and the <strong>California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA)</strong> as amended by the <strong>California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA)</strong>.</li></ul><p>This policy explains how we collect, process, store, disclose and safeguard your personal data when you visit our website, order from us, start a plan or contact our customer care.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_g6nYeY": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Who we are",
            "title": "2. Data controller",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>KARMICA BV in Bruges is responsible for your personal data. Every privacy question goes to one address: </strong><a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a><strong>.</strong></p><p>The data controller responsible for the processing of your personal data is:</p><p><strong>KARMICA BV,</strong> Vizierstraat 28, 8000 Bruges, Belgium · Company and VAT number BE 0676.972.896 · Register of Legal Persons: Enterprise Court of Ghent, division Bruges · <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a></p><p>For all questions, privacy requests or to exercise your rights under the GDPR, write to our Data Privacy Lead at <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a>.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_iDEfUH": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Data we process",
            "title": "3. Personal data we process",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>We collect what we need to deliver your order, run your plan and answer your questions, and no health data.</strong></p><p>Depending on how you interact with KARMICARE, we process the following categories of personal data:</p><ul><li><strong>Identification and contact data:</strong> first name, last name, billing and delivery address, email address, telephone number, and company name or VAT number (for B2B dental partners).</li><li><strong>Transaction and order data: </strong>what you ordered, your plan (Awake and Asleep frequency, interval, delivery cycle), order history, payment reference IDs, carrier, order notes and return or refund records. Full card numbers are processed by our PCI-DSS Level 1 payment providers, Stripe and PayPal, and are never stored on our servers.</li><li><strong>Account and plan data:</strong> customer portal login, delivery schedule preferences, skipped deliveries and plan status (active, paused, cancelled).</li><li><strong>Communication data:</strong> records of your messages by email, contact form or phone, including product questions, after-sales questions and feedback.</li><li><strong>Marketing and newsletter data: </strong>email address, first name, communication preferences, newsletter status, open and click events, and discount or voucher use.</li><li><strong>Technical, navigation and cookie data:</strong> IP address (anonymised where applicable), browser and version, device identifier, operating system, referral source, pages viewed, time per page, language, Day/Night preference and cart token.</li></ul><p>We do <strong>not </strong>process special categories of personal data (Article 9 GDPR), such as racial or ethnic origin, genetic or biometric data, or medical or dental health records. Our formulas are notified EU cosmetics, not medicinal treatments.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_FcEDdA": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Purposes",
            "title": "4. Purposes and legal bases",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Every use of your data rests on a legal basis: your contract, a legal duty, a legitimate interest or your consent.</strong></p><p>Under Article 6 GDPR, we only process your personal data when a valid legal basis exists:</p>",
            "block_content": "<p><strong>Order processing and fulfilment</strong> Processing orders, delivering, sending order updates and managing returns.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> identification, contact, transaction, order<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR)</p><p><strong>Plan management</strong> Managing recurring deliveries of the Duo, processing renewals and providing the customer portal.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> account, plan, transaction, contact<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR)</p><p><strong>Payment processing and fraud prevention</strong> Authenticating transactions, managing chargebacks and preventing payment fraud.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> transaction, identification, technical<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and legitimate interest in fraud prevention (Art. 6(1)(f))</p><p><strong>Customer care</strong> Handling questions, complaints and legal guarantee claims.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> contact, communication, order<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and legitimate interest in efficient customer care (Art. 6(1)(f))</p><p><strong>Legal and tax obligations</strong> Bookkeeping, invoicing, VAT compliance, product liability and regulatory reporting.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> identification, transaction, invoicing<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR; Belgian Code of Economic Law and Income Tax Code)</p><p><strong>Direct marketing to existing customers</strong> Relevant updates and recommendations about similar KARMICARE products.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> contact, order history<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR and Art. XII.13 WER, “soft opt-in”), with an opt-out in every email</p><p><strong>Newsletter and promotional campaigns</strong> Newsletters and promotional offers to prospects.<br/><strong>Data: </strong>contact, first name, marketing data<br/><strong>Legal basis: </strong>explicit prior consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR)</p><p><strong>Website performance and analytics</strong> Aggregated traffic analysis, conversion tracking, site optimisation and debugging.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> technical, navigation, analytics cookies<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> explicit prior consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and ePrivacy Directive)</p><p><strong>Targeted advertising and retargeting</strong> Measuring ad performance, audience segmentation and relevant social ads.<br/><strong>Data:</strong> marketing cookies, pixel data<br/><strong>Legal basis:</strong> explicit prior consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and ePrivacy Directive)</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_xKcNPj": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Service providers",
            "title": "5. Service providers and recipients",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>We never sell your data. A small set of service providers helps us run the shop, each under a written data processing agreement.</strong></p><p>We never sell, rent or lease your personal data to data brokers or unrelated third parties. We share data strictly on a need-to-know basis with vetted service providers (processors) who act on our written instructions under data processing agreements (DPAs):</p><ul><li><strong>E-commerce and hosting: </strong>Shopify Inc. (Canada / US), e-commerce engine, checkout and order management · Webflow, Inc. (US), website hosting, CMS and CDN · Loop Subscriptions (US / India), plan engine and customer portal.</li><li><strong>Payments:</strong> Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd. (Ireland / US), card, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Bancontact and iDEAL payments · PayPal (Europe) S.à r.l. et Cie, S.C.A. (Luxembourg), alternative payments.</li><li><strong>Email and marketing automation:</strong> Klaviyo, Inc. (US), transactional and promotional email, cart reminders (only if you opted in) and list management.</li><li><strong>Logistics: </strong>fulfilment warehouses and carriers (for example Bpost, DHL Express, PostNL and national postal services), only for shipping and tracking.</li><li><strong>Analytics and optimisation:</strong> Google Ireland Limited (Google Analytics 4), web metrics · Meta Platforms Ireland Ltd. (Meta Pixel), conversion tracking and ad optimisation, with your consent · Hotjar Ltd. (Malta), heatmaps and session analysis, with your consent and keystroke masking · TriplePixel / Triple Whale (US), e-commerce attribution and analytics.</li><li><strong>Authorities:</strong> tax authorities (FPS Finance), customs (EORI BE0676972896), courts or law enforcement, only where the law strictly requires it.</li></ul>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_rnPj6g": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Transfers",
            "title": "6. International data transfers",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>When your data leaves the European Economic Area, it travels under an EU-approved safeguard.</strong></p><p>When personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area (EEA), in particular to the United States, KARMICARE ensures an adequate level of protection in line with Articles 44–49 GDPR:</p><ol><li><strong>Adequacy decisions:</strong> transfers to countries the European Commission recognises as adequate, such as Canada for commercial organisations under PIPEDA.</li><li><strong>EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework (DPF):</strong> where US providers (such as Shopify, Google, Meta, Klaviyo, Stripe and Webflow) are certified under the DPF.</li><li><strong>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs): </strong>where providers are not DPF-certified, transfers follow the Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses (Implementing Decision (EU) 2021/914), with transfer impact assessments and encryption safeguards.</li></ol><p>You can ask for a copy of the relevant safeguards at <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a>.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_EAKJLC": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Retention",
            "title": "7. How long we keep your data",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>We keep your data only as long as the purpose or the law requires, then delete or anonymise it.</strong></p><p>We store personal data only as long as necessary for the purpose it was collected for, or to meet legal retention duties:</p><ul><li><strong>Order, invoicing and accounting records:</strong> kept for 7 years after the end of the financial year (Art. III.86 WER and Art. 315 CIR92).</li><li><strong>Plan records:</strong> kept while your plan is active, then 7 years after it ends, for tax and limitation purposes.</li><li><strong>Customer care messages: </strong>kept for 2 years after resolution, to handle legal guarantee claims and disputes.</li><li><strong>Newsletter and marketing data:</strong> kept until you withdraw consent or unsubscribe. After 24 months of inactivity, your data is removed or archived.</li><li><strong>Analytics and cookie data: </strong>kept for at most 13 months, then deleted or permanently anonymised.</li></ul>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_dGmgBJ": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Your rights",
            "title": "8. Complaints and dispute resolution",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>You can see, correct, delete, move or limit your data, and object to marketing at any time. We answer within one month.</strong></p><p>As a data subject, you have the following rights:</p><ol><li><strong>Access (Art. 15): </strong>ask whether we process your data and receive a free copy of it.</li><li><strong>Rectification (Art. 16):</strong> have inaccurate data corrected or incomplete data completed.</li><li><strong>Erasure (Art. 17): </strong>have your data deleted when it is no longer needed, when you withdraw consent or when processing is unlawful, subject to legal retention duties (for example the Belgian 7-year accounting rules).</li><li><strong>Restriction (Art. 18): </strong>have processing frozen while the accuracy or lawfulness of the data is contested.</li><li><strong>Portability (Art. 20):</strong> receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format (JSON, CSV) and have it transferred to another provider.</li><li><strong>Objection (Art. 21): </strong>object at any time, without giving a reason, to direct marketing, and object to processing based on legitimate interests on grounds relating to your situation.</li><li><strong>Withdrawing consent (Art. 7(3)):</strong> withdraw consent for newsletters or marketing cookies at any time, without affecting earlier processing.</li><li><strong>No automated decisions (Art. 22): </strong>KARMICARE does not use automated decision-making or profiling that produces legal effects for you.</li></ol><p><strong>How to exercise your rights</strong></p><p>Email <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> or write to <strong>KARMICA BV — Privacy Operations,</strong> Vizierstraat 28, 8000 Bruges, Belgium.<br/><br/>We respond without undue delay and at the latest within one month of receipt. Where necessary, given the complexity and number of requests, this can be extended by two further months; we then tell you within the first month.</p><p><strong>Your right to complain</strong></p><p>If you believe our processing breaks data protection law, you can lodge a complaint with the Belgian Data Protection Authority or with the supervisory authority in your country:<br/><br/><strong>Belgian Data Protection Authority</strong> (Gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit / Autorité de protection des données), Drukpersstraat 35, 1000 Brussels, Belgium · Tel. +32 2 274 48 00 · <a href=\"mailto:contact@apd-gba.be\" target=\"_blank\">contact@apd-gba.be</a> · <a href=\"https://www.gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit.be\" target=\"_blank\">gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit.be</a></p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_CDtWCV": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Cookies",
            "title": "9. Cookies and tracking",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Essential cookies keep the shop working. Everything else waits for your consent, and you can change your mind at any time.</strong></p><p>Our website uses cookies and similar technologies (local storage, session tokens, pixel tags) to make the site work, remember your preferences and, with your consent, measure traffic and show relevant advertising.<br/><br/><strong>9.1 Cookie categories</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Strictly necessary: </strong>core operation of the shop, security, sessions, cart and checkout. These need no consent and cannot be switched off (Art. 5(3) ePrivacy Directive exemption).</li><li><strong>Functional:</strong> remember your language (en, nl, fr), country and Day/Night preference.</li><li><strong>Performance and analytics: </strong>measure traffic, referrers and site performance (for example Google Analytics 4, Hotjar). Active only after your explicit consent.</li><li><strong>Marketing and advertising:</strong> set by advertising partners (for example Meta Pixel, TriplePixel, Klaviyo) to track visits across websites and build interest profiles for targeted ads. Active only after your explicit consent.</li></ul><p><strong>9.2 Your consent choices</strong></p><p>On your first visit, our consent banner lets you accept all cookies, decline all non-essential cookies, or choose by category.<br/><br/>No non-essential cookies or tracking scripts run before you opt in. You can change or withdraw your choice at any time through the “Cookie settings” link in our footer.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_at3pLy": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "International visitors",
            "title": "10. International visitors",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Visitors from California and the United Kingdom get the same protection, plus the rights their own laws add.</strong></p><p><strong>10.1 California residents (CCPA / CPRA)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Notice at collection:</strong> we collect the identifiers and commercial transaction data listed in section 3 for the purposes described in section 4.</li><li><strong>No sale for money:</strong> KARMICARE does not sell personal data for monetary consideration. Where analytics or advertising cookies count as “sharing” or “targeted advertising” under California law, you can opt out in our cookie banner or with the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal in your browser.</li><li><strong>Your rights:</strong> access, correction, deletion and non-discrimination. Write to <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> with the subject line “California Privacy Request”.</li></ul><p><strong>10.2 United Kingdom visitors (UK GDPR)</strong></p><p>If you live in the United Kingdom, the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 apply, and every reference to the GDPR in this policy applies equally to the UK GDPR. If you are not satisfied with our answer to a privacy request, you can complain to the <strong>UK Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO)</strong> at <a href=\"https://ico.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_qyyKHX": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Security",
            "title": "11. Data security",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Your data travels encrypted, and only the people who need it can reach it.</strong></p><p>KARMICA BV uses technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against accidental loss, unauthorised access, destruction, misuse or alteration:</p><p></p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_pjNTAq": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Changes",
            "title": "12. Changes to this policy",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>When this policy changes, the date at the top changes too, and we tell you first about anything important.</strong></p><p>We may update this policy to reflect changes in how we work, new formulas or new law. The “Last updated” date at the top shows when the latest changes took effect. We announce material changes on our website, or by email to account holders, before they apply.<br/><br/>Questions about your data? Write to <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a>. A person reads every message.</p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        }
      },
